    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Horan Estates present 31 Oakcourt Park to the market - a well-proportioned 3 bedroom bungalow with the added benefit of a self-contained 1 bedroom unit to the rear, offering rental income potential of approximately €1,300 per month. This makes the property a rare and attractive option for investors, multi-generational families, or owner-occupiers looking to offset their mortgage with rental income.\r\n\r\nThe main house comprises a bright living room, a well-fitted kitchen/dining area that opens onto a large rear patio, three bedrooms, and a family bathroom. The layout is practical and comfortable, suited equally to a growing family or those seeking a turnkey home in a quiet setting.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the self-contained 1 bedroom unit offers its own separate living space, bedroom, and bathroom - fully independent from the main house, with its own access. Currently vacant, this unit represents excellent income potential for a buyer looking to offset their monthly outgoings through rental, or for use as additional guest or family accommodation.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from a private driveway to the front with parking for multiple cars, and a generous, fully enclosed patio to the rear.\r\n\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nOakcourt Park is a mature, highly sought-after residential development in the heart of Palmerstown, Dublin 20, known for its quiet, tucked-away feel. The area is well served by everyday amenities, including Palmerstown Shopping Centre and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, both within easy reach, alongside a good selection of local pubs, cafés, and shops. Families are well catered for with a choice of local schools, sports clubs, and leisure facilities nearby.\r\n\r\nFor commuters, the location is hard to beat - the N4 and M50 are just minutes away by car, giving quick access to the city centre and the wider motorway network, while regular bus routes connect the area to Dublin city centre and surrounding areas including Chapelizod, Ballyfermot, and Lucan.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the space, layout, and income potential on offer.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, furniture, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs are provided for guidance only. Furniture shown is for representation purposes only; please consult the estate agent to confirm what will remain in the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Main House\r\n\r\nThe main house is entered via a welcoming hallway (3.04 sqm / 2.51m x 1.21m), which leads through to the heart of the home.\r\n\r\nThe living room (13.13 sqm / 3.52m x 3.73m) is bright and spacious, with a feature fireplace and ample room for a full suite of furniture - a comfortable space to relax or entertain.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen/dining area (9.16 sqm / 2.54m x 3.61m) is well-fitted with a good run of storage and countertop space, and opens directly onto the rear patio - ideal for indoor-outdoor living and entertaining in the warmer months.\r\n\r\nThere are three bedrooms in the main house:\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (9.23 sqm / 3.49m x 2.65m) - a generous double bedroom\r\nBedroom 2 (6.55 sqm / 2.51m x 2.61m) - a further well-proportioned double\r\nBedroom 3 (5.38 sqm / 2.51m x 2.15m) - a versatile single or box room, ideal as a child's room, home office, or nursery\r\n\r\nA central hallway (2.39 sqm / 0.86m x 2.77m) connects the bedrooms to the family bathroom (4.17 sqm / 2.54m x 1.80m), which is fitted with a bath, WC, and wash hand basin, along with a handy closet for additional storage.\r\n\r\nSelf-Contained Unit (to the rear)\r\n\r\nAccessed separately from the main house, this self-contained unit is currently vacant and offers genuinely independent living accommodation with excellent income potential, estimated at approximately €1,300 per month.\r\n\r\nThe living room (15.39 sqm / 5.20m x 3.91m) is the standout feature of the unit - a bright, generously sized open space suitable for living, dining, and kitchen use combined.\r\n\r\nThe bedroom (6.05 sqm / 3.49m x 1.73m) is a comfortable double, positioned just off the main living space.\r\n\r\nA compact bathroom (1.71 sqm / 0.83m x 2.06m) completes the unit, fitted with a WC and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nTotal floor area: approx. 76.2 sqm (820 sqft) across both units"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "3 bedroom bungalow plus a self-contained 1 bedroom unit to the rear\r\nSelf-contained unit offers rental income potential of approx. €1,300 per month\r\nGenerous corner plot with private driveway parking for multiple cars\r\nExtended kitchen/dining area opening onto a large rear patio\r\nTurnkey condition, some cosmetic updating throughout\r\nQuiet, mature cul-de-sac setting in the heart of Palmerstown\r\nExcellent investment or multi-generational living opportunity\r\nClose to Palmerstown Shopping Centre and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre\r\nEasy access to N4 and M50, with regular bus routes to the city centre"
      },
      {
